reply_data.body:
The code regarding 'mini.statusline' looks correct. The warning can be ignored: `require('mini.statusline').setup()` will create `_G.MiniStatusline` global variable which can be used instead of `require('mini.statusline')`, but LuaLS doesn't understand that.

If you don't like that, you can do something like this:

```lua
      local statusline = require('mini.statusline')
      statusline.setup({
        content = {
          active = function()
            local mode, mode_hl = statusline.section_mode({ trunc_width = 120 })
            -- ...
          end,
        }
      })
```

Statusline structure is defined [via defining function for active and inactive windows](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/48f48e4b3f317e9da34ee7a01958b4c5018e2d34/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L9-L13). Each such function should return a string which is treated as a value of 'statusline' option (i.e. see `:h 'statusline'` for special placeholders it may use).

The definition is done by setting [`config.content.active` and/or `config.content.inactive`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/48f48e4b3f317e9da34ee7a01958b4c5018e2d34/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L141-L148). The default value to use as a reference is described [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/48f48e4b3f317e9da34ee7a01958b4c5018e2d34/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L82).

